/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Leviticus chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("leviticus", [
{n:1, name:"The Burnt Offering",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 1:4",verse:"And he shall put his hand upon the head of the burnt offering; and it shall be accepted for him to make atonement for him."},
 facts:["Did you know the burnt offering was the only sacrifice burned entirely on the altar, with nothing kept back for the priest or the offerer? (Leviticus 1:9)","Did you know the offerer laid his own hand on the animal's head, joining himself to the substitute before it died? (Leviticus 1:4)","Did you know even the poor could draw near, since turtledoves or young pigeons were accepted as a burnt offering? (Leviticus 1:14)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"To whom did the LORD speak out of the tabernacle of the congregation?", options:["Moses","Aaron","Joshua","Eleazar"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:1",verse:"And the LORD called unto Moses, and spake unto him out of the tabernacle of the congregation, saying,",
   insight:"God spoke His law through Moses, the mediator He chose. Formation often begins by listening to the voice God has appointed."},
  {q:"From what two groups of animals was an Israelite to bring his offering?", options:["Of the cattle, even of the herd, and of the flock","Of the wild beasts and the birds of prey","Of the creeping things and the fishes","Of whatever animal he happened to find first"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:2",verse:"Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, If any man of you bring an offering unto the LORD, ye shall bring your offering of the cattle, even of the herd, and of the flock.",
   insight:"The offering came from the herds and flocks God had entrusted to them. Worship costs something real, given back from what God first gave."},
  {q:"What kind of animal from the herd was required for a burnt sacrifice?", options:["A male without blemish","A female of any condition","A young animal, blemished or not","The weakest animal of the herd"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:3",verse:"If his offering be a burnt sacrifice of the herd, let him offer a male without blemish: he shall offer it of his own voluntary will at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD.",
   insight:"Only a male without blemish would do. God deserves our best, not our leftovers."},
  {q:"Where was the offerer to present the burnt offering of the herd?", options:["At the door of the tabernacle of the congregation","At the gate of his own house","At the edge of the camp","On any high hill he chose"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:3",verse:"If his offering be a burnt sacrifice of the herd, let him offer a male without blemish: he shall offer it of his own voluntary will at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD.",
   insight:"The offering was presented at God's appointed door, and of his own voluntary will. Approach to God happens on His terms, with a willing heart."},
  {q:"What did the offerer lay upon the head of the burnt offering?", options:["His hand","A crown of olive branches","The priest's staff","A cloth of fine linen"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:4",verse:"And he shall put his hand upon the head of the burnt offering; and it shall be accepted for him to make atonement for him.",
   insight:"Laying his hand on the animal joined the offerer to the sacrifice. In Christ, our sins were laid on Him, and His righteousness is counted as ours."},
  {q:"What did laying his hand on the offering accomplish for the offerer?", options:["It was accepted for him to make atonement for him","It marked the animal as his personal property","It showed the priests that he was wealthy","It proved he had memorized the law"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:4",verse:"And he shall put his hand upon the head of the burnt offering; and it shall be accepted for him to make atonement for him.",
   insight:"The substitute was accepted so atonement could be made. Forgiveness has always come through a substitute God accepts."},
  {q:"Who killed the bullock of the burnt offering?", options:["The offerer himself, before the LORD","Only the high priest, working alone","A Levite chosen by lot","The elders of the city"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:5",verse:"And he shall kill the bullock before the LORD: and the priests, Aaron’s sons, shall bring the blood, and sprinkle the blood round about upon the altar that is by the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.",
   insight:"The offerer did the killing with his own hands. Sin is costly, and facing that cost personally keeps repentance honest."},
  {q:"What did Aaron's sons do with the blood of the bullock?", options:["Brought the blood and sprinkled it round about upon the altar","Poured it out on the ground outside the camp","Kept it in a basin for seven days","Mixed it with oil for anointing"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:5",verse:"And he shall kill the bullock before the LORD: and the priests, Aaron’s sons, shall bring the blood, and sprinkle the blood round about upon the altar that is by the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.",
   insight:"The blood, the life of the sacrifice, was presented to God at the altar. Life for life: that is the price of atonement."},
  {q:"What was done to the burnt offering after it was killed?", options:["He flayed it and cut it into his pieces","He buried it whole outside the camp","He gave the hide to the poor","He burned it without any preparation"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:6",verse:"And he shall flay the burnt offering, and cut it into his pieces.",
   insight:"The offering was prepared carefully, piece by piece. God is not honored by careless worship."},
  {q:"What did the sons of Aaron put on the altar?", options:["Fire upon the altar, and wood in order upon the fire","Water and hyssop for cleansing","Incense and sweet spices only","Nothing, for fire fell from heaven each time"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:7",verse:"And the sons of Aaron the priest shall put fire upon the altar, and lay the wood in order upon the fire:",
   insight:"The priests tended the fire and laid the wood in order. Faithful, ordinary preparation is part of serving God."},
  {q:"What did the priests lay in order upon the wood?", options:["The parts, the head, and the fat","Only the skin and the bones","The blood and the water","The horns and the hooves"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:8",verse:"And the priests, Aaron’s sons, shall lay the parts, the head, and the fat, in order upon the wood that is on the fire which is upon the altar:",
   insight:"Every part was arranged with care on the altar. God receives the whole life, laid out before Him in order."},
  {q:"How were the inwards and legs prepared before burning?", options:["They were washed with water","They were rubbed with salt","They were set aside for the priests","They were buried in the ashes"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:9",verse:"But his inwards and his legs shall he wash in water: and the priest shall burn all on the altar, to be a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.",
   insight:"Even the inward parts were washed clean. God cares about inner purity, not just outward show."},
  {q:"What did the burning of the offering become to the LORD?", options:["A sweet savour unto the LORD","A bitter smoke of judgment","A memorial of Israel's rebellion","A common meal for the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:9",verse:"But his inwards and his legs shall he wash in water: and the priest shall burn all on the altar, to be a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.",
   insight:"The fully surrendered offering pleased God like a sweet aroma. A life wholly given to Him is still a delight to Him."},
  {q:"What animals could be offered as a burnt sacrifice from the flocks?", options:["Sheep or goats, a male without blemish","Only doves and pigeons","Any clean animal, male or female","Oxen and camels"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:10",verse:"And if his offering be of the flocks, namely, of the sheep, or of the goats, for a burnt sacrifice; he shall bring it a male without blemish.",
   insight:"The standard never lowered: male, without blemish. God's holiness does not bend to our convenience."},
  {q:"On which side of the altar was the flock offering killed?", options:["On the side of the altar northward, before the LORD","On the south side, facing toward Egypt","Inside the holy place","Outside the camp by the ash heap"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:11",verse:"And he shall kill it on the side of the altar northward before the LORD: and the priests, Aaron’s sons, shall sprinkle his blood round about upon the altar.",
   insight:"Even the place of killing was appointed. Details matter to God, because He is a God of order."},
  {q:"What birds could the poor offer as a burnt sacrifice?", options:["Turtledoves or young pigeons","Eagles or hawks","Sparrows or ravens","Any bird caught in a snare"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:14",verse:"And if the burnt sacrifice for his offering to the LORD be of fowls, then he shall bring his offering of turtledoves, or of young pigeons.",
   insight:"God made a way for the poor to draw near. No one is priced out of His mercy."},
  {q:"What did the priest wring off the bird?", options:["His head","His wings","His feet","His tail"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:15",verse:"And the priest shall bring it unto the altar, and wring off his head, and burn it on the altar; and the blood thereof shall be wrung out at the side of the altar:",
   insight:"The bird's head was wrung off and burned on the altar. Small offering or great, the same atonement was needed."},
  {q:"Where was the bird's blood wrung out?", options:["At the side of the altar","On the horns of the altar","In the laver of water","Outside the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:15",verse:"And the priest shall bring it unto the altar, and wring off his head, and burn it on the altar; and the blood thereof shall be wrung out at the side of the altar:",
   insight:"The bird's blood was wrung out at the side of the altar. Every drop of the sacrifice was presented to God."},
  {q:"Where was the bird's crop with its feathers cast?", options:["Beside the altar on the east side, by the place of the ashes","Into the fire with the rest of the bird","Outside the camp at midnight","Into the laver of water"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:16",verse:"And he shall pluck away his crop with his feathers, and cast it beside the altar on the east part, by the place of the ashes:",
   insight:"The crop and feathers were removed to the ash heap. God separates what defiles from what is offered to Him."},
  {q:"How was the bird to be cloven?", options:["Cleave it with the wings thereof, but not divide it asunder","Tear it in two from head to tail","Pluck it clean and burn it whole","Cut off the wings and burn them separately"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 1:17",verse:"And he shall cleave it with the wings thereof, but shall not divide it asunder: and the priest shall burn it upon the altar, upon the wood that is upon the fire: it is a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.",
   insight:"The bird was cloven with its wings but not divided asunder. Even in judgment, God's instructions carried restraint and care."}
 ]},
{n:2, name:"The Grain Offering",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 2:13",verse:"And every oblation of thy meat offering shalt thou season with salt; neither shalt thou suffer the salt of the covenant of thy God to be lacking from thy meat offering: with all thine offerings thou shalt offer salt."},
 facts:["Did you know the burned handful of the grain offering was called a memorial, while the rest fed Aaron and his sons? (Leviticus 2:2-3)","Did you know no leaven or honey was ever burned on the altar, though firstfruits could be presented in another way? (Leviticus 2:11-12)","Did you know every grain offering was seasoned with salt, called the salt of the covenant of God? (Leviticus 2:13)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"What was the basic ingredient of the meat offering?", options:["Fine flour","Coarse barley meal","Crushed olives","Ground lentils"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:1",verse:"And when any will offer a meat offering unto the LORD, his offering shall be of fine flour; and he shall pour oil upon it, and put frankincense thereon:",
   insight:"The offering began with fine flour, the best of the harvest carefully ground. God is worthy of our finest work, not our coarse leftovers."},
  {q:"What two things were put upon the fine flour?", options:["Oil and frankincense","Water and salt","Honey and wine","Milk and butter"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:1",verse:"And when any will offer a meat offering unto the LORD, his offering shall be of fine flour; and he shall pour oil upon it, and put frankincense thereon:",
   insight:"Oil and frankincense crowned the flour. The Spirit's richness and prayer's fragrance belong over everything we offer."},
  {q:"To whom was the meat offering brought?", options:["To Aaron's sons the priests","To the elders of the city","To the keeper of the treasury","To any Levite passing by"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:2",verse:"And he shall bring it to Aaron’s sons the priests: and he shall take thereout his handful of the flour thereof, and of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof; and the priest shall burn the memorial of it upon the altar, to be an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD:",
   insight:"The offering was brought to the priests, God's appointed servants. Worship is never a solo act; God gives us ministers."},
  {q:"How much of the flour and oil did the priest take to burn?", options:["His handful of the flour thereof, and of the oil thereof","The entire offering, leaving nothing","Exactly half, measured by weight","Only a pinch between two fingers"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:2",verse:"And he shall bring it to Aaron’s sons the priests: and he shall take thereout his handful of the flour thereof, and of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof; and the priest shall burn the memorial of it upon the altar, to be an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD:",
   insight:"A handful was burned as God's portion. A small, deliberate gift, set apart for God, carries great weight."},
  {q:"Who received the remnant of the meat offering?", options:["Aaron's and his sons'","The poor of the congregation","The stranger within the gates","The offerer and his household"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:3",verse:"And the remnant of the meat offerings shall be Aaron’s and his sons’: it is a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.",
   insight:"What remained fed Aaron and his sons. God provides for those who serve Him at the altar."},
  {q:"How holy was the remnant of the offering called?", options:["Most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire","Common food for ordinary days","Clean but not consecrated","Holy only on the Sabbath"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:3",verse:"And the remnant of the meat offerings shall be Aaron’s and his sons’: it is a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.",
   insight:"The remnant was called most holy. Even the portion used for daily bread was sacred when it belonged to God."},
  {q:"What two forms could an oven-baked meat offering take?", options:["Unleavened cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, or unleavened wafers anointed with oil","Leavened loaves or honey cakes","Meat pies or fish pastries","Thick porridge or thin gruel"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:4",verse:"And if thou bring an oblation of a meat offering baken in the oven, it shall be unleavened cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, or unleavened wafers anointed with oil.",
   insight:"Whether cakes or wafers, the baking had to be unleavened. Sincerity without corruption marks an acceptable offering."},
  {q:"What kind of flour was used for an offering baked in a pan?", options:["Fine flour unleavened, mingled with oil","Coarse flour mixed with leaven","Barley flour mixed with honey","Wheat flour mixed with wine"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:5",verse:"And if thy oblation be a meat offering baken in a pan, it shall be of fine flour unleavened, mingled with oil.",
   insight:"The pan offering was fine flour unleavened, mingled with oil. Simplicity, offered purely, pleases God."},
  {q:"What was done to the pan offering before oil was poured on it?", options:["Part it in pieces, and pour oil thereon","Knead it a second time","Let it rise overnight","Sprinkle it with wine"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:6",verse:"Thou shalt part it in pieces, and pour oil thereon: it is a meat offering.",
   insight:"The offering was broken into pieces before the oil was poured on. Brokenness comes before the Spirit's anointing."},
  {q:"What vessel is named for the offering of verse 7?", options:["The fryingpan","The cauldron","The kettle","The earthen pot"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:7",verse:"And if thy oblation be a meat offering baken in the frying pan, it shall be made of fine flour with oil.",
   insight:"God accepted offerings from the oven, the pan, and the fryingpan. He meets worship in the kitchen we actually have."},
  {q:"To whom was the prepared meat offering presented?", options:["Unto the priest, who brought it unto the altar","Unto the king, who tasted it first","Unto the elders, who divided it","Unto the offerer, who ate it at home"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:8",verse:"And thou shalt bring the meat offering that is made of these things unto the LORD: and when it is presented unto the priest, he shall bring it unto the altar.",
   insight:"The prepared gift was presented to the priest, who brought it to the altar. Preparation ends in presentation; we bring our work to God."},
  {q:"What did the priest take from the meat offering to burn?", options:["A memorial thereof","The whole of it at once","Only the frankincense","Only the salt"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:9",verse:"And the priest shall take from the meat offering a memorial thereof, and shall burn it upon the altar: it is an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.",
   insight:"The burned portion was a memorial before God. Our gifts remind Him of our devotion, and remind us of His provision."},
  {q:"What was left of the meat offering for Aaron and his sons?", options:["That which was left, called most holy of the offerings of the LORD","Only the crumbs that fell from the altar","Nothing, for all was burned","The oil and frankincense alone"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:10",verse:"And that which is left of the meat offering shall be Aaron’s and his sons’: it is a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.",
   insight:"Again the remnant fed the priests, called most holy. Repetition in Scripture is emphasis: God truly cares for His servants."},
  {q:"What two things were never to be burned in an offering made by fire?", options:["Leaven and honey","Salt and oil","Flour and frankincense","Water and wine"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:11",verse:"No meat offering, which ye shall bring unto the LORD, shall be made with leaven: for ye shall burn no leaven, nor any honey, in any offering of the LORD made by fire.",
   insight:"Leaven and honey, pictures of corruption and mere sweetness, were barred from the fire. God wants purity, not flattery."},
  {q:"What could be offered as firstfruits but not burned for a sweet savour?", options:["The oblation of the firstfruits","A leavened thanksgiving loaf","A honey cake of celebration","A meat offering with leaven"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:12",verse:"As for the oblation of the firstfruits, ye shall offer them unto the LORD: but they shall not be burnt on the altar for a sweet savour.",
   insight:"Firstfruits could be presented but not burned for a sweet savour. Some gifts honor God best by being given, not consumed."},
  {q:"With what was every meat offering to be seasoned?", options:["With salt","With honey","With bitter herbs","With sweet spices"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:13",verse:"And every oblation of thy meat offering shalt thou season with salt; neither shalt thou suffer the salt of the covenant of thy God to be lacking from thy meat offering: with all thine offerings thou shalt offer salt.",
   insight:"Every offering was seasoned with salt. Our devotion should have preserving, distinctive flavor, never bland."},
  {q:"To what covenant was the salt tied?", options:["The salt of the covenant of thy God","The covenant made with Abraham alone","The covenant of the Sabbath day","The covenant of circumcision"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:13",verse:"And every oblation of thy meat offering shalt thou season with salt; neither shalt thou suffer the salt of the covenant of thy God to be lacking from thy meat offering: with all thine offerings thou shalt offer salt.",
   insight:"The salt recalled God's covenant. Faithfulness, like salt, keeps what is good from spoiling."},
  {q:"What form did the firstfruits meat offering take?", options:["Green ears of corn dried by the fire, even corn beaten out of full ears","Ripe grapes crushed into new wine","Dried figs pressed into cakes","Parched wheat mixed with honey"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:14",verse:"And if thou offer a meat offering of thy firstfruits unto the LORD, thou shalt offer for the meat offering of thy firstfruits green ears of corn dried by the fire, even corn beaten out of full ears.",
   insight:"The firstfruits came as green ears dried by fire, beaten from full ears. The first and best of the harvest belonged to God."},
  {q:"What was put upon the firstfruits offering?", options:["Oil and frankincense","Water and hyssop","Leaven and honey","Milk and butter"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:15",verse:"And thou shalt put oil upon it, and lay frankincense thereon: it is a meat offering.",
   insight:"Oil and frankincense dressed even the simple grain. The Spirit and prayer dignify the humblest gift."},
  {q:"What was burned as the memorial of the firstfruits?", options:["Part of the beaten corn, part of the oil, with all the frankincense","The whole sheaf, bound with cords","Only the husks and the chaff","A single grain from each ear"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 2:16",verse:"And the priest shall burn the memorial of it, part of the beaten corn thereof, and part of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof: it is an offering made by fire unto the LORD.",
   insight:"Part of the corn, part of the oil, and all the frankincense went up in fire to the LORD. God claims the first portion as His own."}
 ]},
{n:3, name:"The Peace Offering",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 3:16",verse:"And the priest shall burn them upon the altar: it is the food of the offering made by fire for a sweet savour: all the fat is the LORD’S."},
 facts:["Did you know the peace offering was the fellowship meal of the sacrifices, with part burned to God as food of the offering and part shared as a meal? (Leviticus 3:11)","Did you know all the fat belonged to the LORD, a perpetual rule for Israel in all their dwellings? (Leviticus 3:16-17)","Did you know the offerer laid his hand on the animal's head even in this joyful offering, showing fellowship still rests on atonement? (Leviticus 3:2)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"If the peace offering was of the herd, what was required?", options:["Male or female, without blemish","Only a male, without blemish","Only a female, without blemish","Any animal, blemished or not"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:1",verse:"And if his oblation be a sacrifice of peace offering, if he offer it of the herd; whether it be a male or female, he shall offer it without blemish before the LORD.",
   insight:"The peace offering could be male or female, but never blemished. Fellowship with God is open to all, yet never casual."},
  {q:"Where did the offerer lay his hand for the herd peace offering?", options:["Upon the head of his offering","Upon the horns of the altar","Upon the priest's hands","Upon the door of the tabernacle"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:2",verse:"And he shall lay his hand upon the head of his offering, and kill it at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aaron’s sons the priests shall sprinkle the blood upon the altar round about.",
   insight:"Even in this joyful offering, the offerer laid his hand on the animal's head. Fellowship with God still rests on atonement."},
  {q:"Where was the herd peace offering killed?", options:["At the door of the tabernacle of the congregation","In the middle of the camp","On the north side of the altar","Outside the camp by the ashes"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:2",verse:"And he shall lay his hand upon the head of his offering, and kill it at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aaron’s sons the priests shall sprinkle the blood upon the altar round about.",
   insight:"The peace offering was killed at the door of the tabernacle. Joy in God's presence begins at the place of sacrifice."},
  {q:"What fat of the peace offering was offered by fire to the LORD?", options:["The fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that is upon the inwards","Only the fat of the legs","The fat mixed with the blood","None of the fat at all"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:3",verse:"And he shall offer of the sacrifice of the peace offering an offering made by fire unto the LORD; the fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that is upon the inwards,",
   insight:"The fat covering the inwards went to God. The richest part belonged to Him, a sign He deserves the best of our inward life."},
  {q:"Which inner organs are named in the peace offering?", options:["The two kidneys, and the caul above the liver","The heart and the lungs","The stomach and the intestines","The spleen and the gall"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:4",verse:"And the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, which is by the flanks, and the caul above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away.",
   insight:"The kidneys and the caul above the liver were set apart. God claims the hidden, inner parts, not just what shows."},
  {q:"Upon what was the peace offering burned?", options:["Upon the burnt sacrifice, which is upon the wood that is on the fire","Upon the bare ground outside the camp","Upon the altar of incense","Upon a separate altar in the courtyard"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:5",verse:"And Aaron’s sons shall burn it on the altar upon the burnt sacrifice, which is upon the wood that is on the fire: it is an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.",
   insight:"The peace offering burned upon the burnt sacrifice. Fellowship with God rests on full surrender to Him."},
  {q:"What did the burning of the peace offering become to the LORD?", options:["An offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD","A bitter smoke of judgment","A memorial of rebellion","A common meal for the priests"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:5",verse:"And Aaron’s sons shall burn it on the altar upon the burnt sacrifice, which is upon the wood that is on the fire: it is an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.",
   insight:"The offering rose as a sweet savour. Reconciled fellowship delights the heart of God."},
  {q:"If the peace offering was of the flock, what was required?", options:["Male or female, without blemish","Only a male lamb","Only a female goat","Any sheep or goat at hand"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:6",verse:"And if his offering for a sacrifice of peace offering unto the LORD be of the flock; male or female, he shall offer it without blemish.",
   insight:"From the flock as from the herd, male or female without blemish. God's table is wide, but His standard is unchanged."},
  {q:"If a man offered a lamb for his offering, what was he to do?", options:["Offer it before the LORD","Keep it in his own tent","Give it to the poor alive","Set it free in the wilderness"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:7",verse:"If he offer a lamb for his offering, then shall he offer it before the LORD.",
   insight:"A lamb was offered before the LORD. The gentle lamb at the altar foreshadows the Lamb who takes away sin."},
  {q:"Where was the lamb of the peace offering killed?", options:["Before the tabernacle of the congregation","At the door of the offerer's tent","On the east side of the camp","Inside the holy place"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:8",verse:"And he shall lay his hand upon the head of his offering, and kill it before the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aaron’s sons shall sprinkle the blood thereof round about upon the altar.",
   insight:"The lamb died before the tabernacle of the congregation. Our peace was made in God's presence, at a cost."},
  {q:"What did Aaron's sons do with the lamb's blood?", options:["Sprinkled the blood thereof round about upon the altar","Poured it into the laver","Sprinkled it seven times before the veil","Carried it outside the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:8",verse:"And he shall lay his hand upon the head of his offering, and kill it before the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aaron’s sons shall sprinkle the blood thereof round about upon the altar.",
   insight:"The blood was sprinkled round about upon the altar. Peace with God is sealed in blood, not in good intentions."},
  {q:"What extra rich portion was taken from the sheep's peace offering?", options:["The whole rump, taken off hard by the backbone","The head with the horns","The legs with the hooves","The skin with the wool"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:9",verse:"And he shall offer of the sacrifice of the peace offering an offering made by fire unto the LORD; the fat thereof, and the whole rump, it shall he take off hard by the backbone; and the fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that is upon the inwards,",
   insight:"The whole rump, the rich tail portion, was taken off for God. Nothing rich or choice is wasted when given to Him."},
  {q:"Where was the fat upon the kidneys in the sheep offering?", options:["Upon them by the flanks","Underneath the backbone","Around the neck","Inside the chest"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:10",verse:"And the two kidneys, and the fat that is upon them, which is by the flanks, and the caul above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away.",
   insight:"The fat upon the kidneys by the flanks was removed for God. He sees and claims the parts we hide."},
  {q:"What did the priest's burning make the peace offering?", options:["The food of the offering made by fire unto the LORD","A meal for the priests alone","A gift returned to the offerer","An offering for the stranger"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:11",verse:"And the priest shall burn it upon the altar: it is the food of the offering made by fire unto the LORD.",
   insight:"The burned portion was called food of the offering made by fire. God invites us to think of sacrifice as a shared meal."},
  {q:"If his offering was a goat, what was he to do?", options:["Offer it before the LORD","Offer it in his own field","Give it to the Levites alive","Exchange it for a lamb"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:12",verse:"And if his offering be a goat, then he shall offer it before the LORD.",
   insight:"A goat could also be a peace offering before the LORD. God accepts sincere worship in more than one form."},
  {q:"What did the offerer do to the goat before killing it?", options:["Lay his hand upon the head of it","Anoint its head with oil","Tie a scarlet cord to its horn","Wash its feet with water"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:13",verse:"And he shall lay his hand upon the head of it, and kill it before the tabernacle of the congregation: and the sons of Aaron shall sprinkle the blood thereof upon the altar round about.",
   insight:"Hands were laid on the goat's head too. Every path to fellowship passes through identification with the sacrifice."},
  {q:"Where was the goat of the peace offering killed?", options:["Before the tabernacle of the congregation","At the city gate","Beside the altar of incense","In the outer court at noon"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:13",verse:"And he shall lay his hand upon the head of it, and kill it before the tabernacle of the congregation: and the sons of Aaron shall sprinkle the blood thereof upon the altar round about.",
   insight:"The goat was killed before the tabernacle like the rest. There are no shortcuts to peace with God."},
  {q:"What fat of the goat was offered by fire?", options:["The fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that is upon the inwards","Only the fat of the tail","The fat boiled with the meat","None, for goats were exempt"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:14",verse:"And he shall offer thereof his offering, even an offering made by fire unto the LORD; the fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that is upon the inwards,",
   insight:"The fat covering the inwards was God's portion again. Repetition teaches: the best belongs to the LORD."},
  {q:"Whose is all the fat?", options:["The LORD's","The priest's","The offerer's","The king's"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:16",verse:"And the priest shall burn them upon the altar: it is the food of the offering made by fire for a sweet savour: all the fat is the LORD’S.",
   insight:"All the fat is the LORD's. When we grasp that everything is His, giving becomes joy."},
  {q:"What did the perpetual statute forbid Israel to eat?", options:["Fat and blood","Leaven and honey","Pork and shellfish","Bread and wine"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 3:17",verse:"It shall be a perpetual statute for your generations throughout all your dwellings, that ye eat neither fat nor blood.",
   insight:"Israel was to eat neither fat nor blood, in all their dwellings, forever. Some boundaries are permanent because life itself is sacred."}
 ]},
{n:4, name:"The Sin Offering",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 4:20",verse:"And he shall do with the bullock as he did with the bullock for a sin offering, so shall he do with this: and the priest shall make an atonement for them, and it shall be forgiven them."},
 facts:["Did you know the sin offering covered sins committed through ignorance, not open defiance? (Leviticus 4:2)","Did you know the blood was sprinkled seven times before the veil, showing how seriously God treats hidden sin? (Leviticus 4:6)","Did you know the offering changed with the sinner's standing: a bull for the priest, a male goat for a ruler, a female goat or lamb for an ordinary person? (Leviticus 4:3)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"To whom did the LORD speak concerning the sin offering?", options:["Moses","Aaron","Joshua","Eleazar"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:1",verse:"And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,",
   insight:"The LORD spoke to Moses to teach Israel about hidden sins. God lovingly provides a way back before we even ask."},
  {q:"What kind of sin required a sin offering?", options:["A soul sinning through ignorance against the commandments","Only deliberate rebellion","Only sins committed in anger","Only sins witnessed by others"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:2",verse:"Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, If a soul shall sin through ignorance against any of the commandments of the LORD concerning things which ought not to be done, and shall do against any of them:",
   insight:"The sin offering covered sins done through ignorance. Even sins we did not mean still need atonement."},
  {q:"What did the anointed priest bring when he sinned?", options:["A young bullock without blemish unto the LORD","A lamb of the first year","Two turtledoves","A tenth of an ephah of flour"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:3",verse:"If the priest that is anointed do sin according to the sin of the people; then let him bring for his sin, which he hath sinned, a young bullock without blemish unto the LORD for a sin offering.",
   insight:"When the anointed priest sinned, he brought a young bullock without blemish. Leaders need the costliest atonement, because their sin affects the people."},
  {q:"Where did the priest bring the bullock?", options:["Unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD","To the gate of the city","To the top of a nearby hill","To his own house"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:4",verse:"And he shall bring the bullock unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD; and shall lay his hand upon the bullock’s head, and kill the bullock before the LORD.",
   insight:"The bullock was brought to the door of the tabernacle before the LORD. Confession happens in God's presence, not in hiding."},
  {q:"How many times did the priest sprinkle the blood before the veil?", options:["Seven times","Three times","Twelve times","Once"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:6",verse:"And the priest shall dip his finger in the blood, and sprinkle of the blood seven times before the LORD, before the vail of the sanctuary.",
   insight:"The blood was sprinkled seven times before the veil. Complete cleansing is God's answer to complete guilt."},
  {q:"Where did the priest put some of the bullock's blood?", options:["Upon the horns of the altar of sweet incense","Upon the doorposts of the tabernacle","Upon the mercy seat itself","Upon the priest's own forehead"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:7",verse:"And the priest shall put some of the blood upon the horns of the altar of sweet incense before the LORD, which is in the tabernacle of the congregation: and shall pour all the blood of the bullock at the bottom of the altar of the burnt offering, which is at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.",
   insight:"Blood touched the horns of the altar of sweet incense. Atonement reaches even our prayers, which sin corrupts."},
  {q:"Where was the whole bullock burned?", options:["Without the camp, where the ashes are poured out","Inside the holy place","On the altar of incense","In the priest's courtyard"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:12",verse:"Even the whole bullock shall he carry forth without the camp unto a clean place, where the ashes are poured out, and burn him on the wood with fire: where the ashes are poured out shall he be burnt.",
   insight:"The bullock's remains burned outside the camp where ashes were poured out. Sin's shame is carried away from God's holy presence."},
  {q:"When did the whole congregation need a sin offering?", options:["When they sinned through ignorance and it was hid from the eyes of the assembly","Only when the priests commanded a feast","Only after a military defeat","Only at the new moon"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:13",verse:"And if the whole congregation of Israel sin through ignorance, and the thing be hid from the eyes of the assembly, and they have done somewhat against any of the commandments of the LORD concerning things which should not be done, and are guilty;",
   insight:"When the whole assembly sinned unknowingly, they were still guilty. A community can drift together, and must repent together."},
  {q:"What did the congregation offer when their sin was known?", options:["A young bullock for the sin","A ram for a burnt offering","Two goats for the priests","A basket of firstfruits"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:14",verse:"When the sin, which they have sinned against it, is known, then the congregation shall offer a young bullock for the sin, and bring him before the tabernacle of the congregation.",
   insight:"Once the sin was known, the congregation offered a young bullock. Knowledge brings responsibility to act."},
  {q:"Who laid their hands on the bullock's head for the congregation?", options:["The elders of the congregation","The young men of the camp","The priests alone","The ruler and his servants"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:15",verse:"And the elders of the congregation shall lay their hands upon the head of the bullock before the LORD: and the bullock shall be killed before the LORD.",
   insight:"The elders laid their hands on the bullock's head. Leaders represent the people, in guilt and in repentance."},
  {q:"What was the result when the priest made atonement for the congregation?", options:["It shall be forgiven them","They were exiled for a year","They paid a fine of silver","They fasted for seven days"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:20",verse:"And he shall do with the bullock as he did with the bullock for a sin offering, so shall he do with this: and the priest shall make an atonement for them, and it shall be forgiven them.",
   insight:"The priest made atonement, and it was forgiven them. God's promise is sure: true atonement brings true forgiveness."},
  {q:"What was the bullock burned outside the camp called?", options:["A sin offering for the congregation","A burnt offering for the priests","A peace offering for the elders","A memorial for the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:21",verse:"And he shall carry forth the bullock without the camp, and burn him as he burned the first bullock: it is a sin offering for the congregation.",
   insight:"The bullock burned outside the camp was the congregation's sin offering. God removes the sin of His people completely."},
  {q:"Who is described as sinning in verse 22?", options:["A ruler","A prophet","A stranger","A child"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:22",verse:"When a ruler hath sinned, and done somewhat through ignorance against any of the commandments of the LORD his God concerning things which should not be done, and is guilty;",
   insight:"When a ruler sinned through ignorance, he was guilty too. Rank offers no exemption from God's law."},
  {q:"What did the ruler bring when his sin came to his knowledge?", options:["A kid of the goats, a male without blemish","A young bullock","A ewe lamb","Two young pigeons"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:23",verse:"Or if his sin, wherein he hath sinned, come to his knowledge; he shall bring his offering, a kid of the goats, a male without blemish:",
   insight:"The ruler brought a male kid of the goats without blemish. Greater responsibility meant a prescribed, unblemished offering."},
  {q:"Where did the priest put the blood of the ruler's sin offering?", options:["Upon the horns of the altar of the burnt offering","Upon the veil of the sanctuary","Upon the ruler's hands","Upon the city gate"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:25",verse:"And the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put it upon the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out his blood at the bottom of the altar of burnt offering.",
   insight:"The blood went on the horns of the altar of burnt offering. Atonement is applied where sacrifice is made."},
  {q:"What happened after the priest made atonement for the ruler?", options:["It shall be forgiven him","He was removed from office","He offered a second goat","He waited forty days"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:26",verse:"And he shall burn all his fat upon the altar, as the fat of the sacrifice of peace offerings: and the priest shall make an atonement for him as concerning his sin, and it shall be forgiven him.",
   insight:"The priest made atonement for the ruler, and he was forgiven. No one is too high to need mercy, or too high to receive it."},
  {q:"Who is in view when one of the common people sins through ignorance?", options:["Any one of the common people of the land","Only the priests' servants","Only visiting strangers","Only the tribal leaders"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:27",verse:"And if any one of the common people sin through ignorance, while he doeth somewhat against any of the commandments of the LORD concerning things which ought not to be done, and be guilty;",
   insight:"The law reached the common person who sinned through ignorance. God's mercy is not reserved for the prominent."},
  {q:"What did the common person bring when his sin was known?", options:["A kid of the goats, a female without blemish","A young bullock","A male goat","A pair of doves"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:28",verse:"Or if his sin, which he hath sinned, come to his knowledge: then he shall bring his offering, a kid of the goats, a female without blemish, for his sin which he hath sinned.",
   insight:"The ordinary sinner brought a female kid without blemish. God scaled the offering to the sinner, but never lowered His holiness."},
  {q:"What happened when the priest burned the fat for a sweet savour?", options:["The priest made atonement for him, and it shall be forgiven him","The people stoned the sinner","The offering was rejected","The priest kept the fat for himself"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:31",verse:"And he shall take away all the fat thereof, as the fat is taken away from off the sacrifice of peace offerings; and the priest shall burn it upon the altar for a sweet savour unto the LORD; and the priest shall make an atonement for him, and it shall be forgiven him.",
   insight:"The fat burned for a sweet savour, and he was forgiven. Repentance that costs us something pleases God."},
  {q:"If he brought a lamb for his sin offering, what was required?", options:["A female without blemish","A male of the first year","Any lamb, blemished or not","Two lambs together"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 4:32",verse:"And if he bring a lamb for a sin offering, he shall bring it a female without blemish.",
   insight:"A lamb, a female without blemish, could also atone. God provided options so that no willing sinner was turned away."}
 ]},
{n:5, name:"The Trespass Offering",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 5:5",verse:"And it shall be, when he shall be guilty in one of these things, that he shall confess that he hath sinned in that thing:"},
 facts:["Did you know the trespass offering began with confession: the guilty person had to name the sin first? (Leviticus 5:5)","Did you know if someone harmed God's holy things, he repaid the loss plus a fifth part to the priest? (Leviticus 5:16)","Did you know even the poorest could be cleansed, with a handful of flour accepted when birds were out of reach? (Leviticus 5:11)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"What happened to the witness who heard swearing and did not utter it?", options:["He shall bear his iniquity","He was praised for his silence","He paid a small fine","Nothing, for silence was wisdom"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:1",verse:"And if a soul sin, and hear the voice of swearing, and is a witness, whether he hath seen or known of it; if he do not utter it, then he shall bear his iniquity.",
   insight:"Silence made the witness bear his iniquity. Failing to speak truth when it matters is itself a sin."},
  {q:"What made a soul unclean and guilty in verse 2?", options:["Touching the carcase of an unclean beast, cattle, or creeping thing","Eating bread with unwashed hands","Walking through the camp at night","Wearing mixed fabrics"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:2",verse:"Or if a soul touch any unclean thing, whether it be a carcase of an unclean beast, or a carcase of unclean cattle, or the carcase of unclean creeping things, and if it be hidden from him; he also shall be unclean, and guilty.",
   insight:"Touching a carcass brought guilt, even unknowingly. Holiness guards the heart against defilement, intentional or not."},
  {q:"When did touching the uncleanness of man bring guilt?", options:["When it was hid from him, but he came to know it","Only if done on the Sabbath","Only if witnessed by two men","Never, for it was a light matter"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:3",verse:"Or if he touch the uncleanness of man, whatsoever uncleanness it be that a man shall be defiled withal, and it be hid from him; when he knoweth of it, then he shall be guilty.",
   insight:"Hidden uncleanness still made him guilty once known. God calls us to deal with defilement the moment we recognize it."},
  {q:"What rash act of the lips brought guilt?", options:["Swearing to do evil or to do good, pronounced with an oath","Singing a song of praise","Praying aloud in the assembly","Blessing a neighbor"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:4",verse:"Or if a soul swear, pronouncing with his lips to do evil, or to do good, whatsoever it be that a man shall pronounce with an oath, and it be hid from him; when he knoweth of it, then he shall be guilty in one of these.",
   insight:"A rash oath, to do evil or good, brought guilt. Words spoken lightly before God carry heavy weight."},
  {q:"What was the guilty person required to do first?", options:["Confess that he hath sinned in that thing","Bring the offering before confessing","Wait seven days in silence","Pay the priest in silver"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:5",verse:"And it shall be, when he shall be guilty in one of these things, that he shall confess that he hath sinned in that thing:",
   insight:"The guilty one had to confess the specific sin. Naming our sin honestly is where restoration begins."},
  {q:"What did he bring as his trespass offering for his sin?", options:["A female from the flock, a lamb or kid of the goats","A young bullock","Two rams","A basket of grain"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:6",verse:"And he shall bring his trespass offering unto the LORD for his sin which he hath sinned, a female from the flock, a lamb or a kid of the goats, for a sin offering; and the priest shall make an atonement for him concerning his sin.",
   insight:"The trespass offering was a female lamb or goat. God set the price of restoration within reach."},
  {q:"If he could not afford a lamb, what was he to bring?", options:["Two turtledoves or two young pigeons, one for a sin offering and the other for a burnt offering","A single sparrow","Nothing, for he was excused","Only his confession"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:7",verse:"And if he be not able to bring a lamb, then he shall bring for his trespass, which he hath committed, two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, unto the LORD; one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering.",
   insight:"If too poor for a lamb, two birds would do. Poverty never bars anyone from God's forgiveness."},
  {q:"How did the priest offer the bird for the sin offering?", options:["Wring off his head from his neck, but not divide it asunder","Burn it whole without preparation","Pluck it and set it free","Divide it into seven pieces"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:8",verse:"And he shall bring them unto the priest, who shall offer that which is for the sin offering first, and wring off his head from his neck, but shall not divide it asunder:",
   insight:"The bird's head was wrung off but not divided asunder. God's rituals carried meaning in every detail."},
  {q:"What was done with the blood of the bird sin offering?", options:["Sprinkle it upon the side of the altar, and wring out the rest at the bottom","Pour it all on the ground","Sprinkle it on the offerer's head","Keep it for the next day"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:9",verse:"And he shall sprinkle of the blood of the sin offering upon the side of the altar; and the rest of the blood shall be wrung out at the bottom of the altar: it is a sin offering.",
   insight:"Blood was sprinkled on the altar's side, the rest wrung out at its base. Atonement was applied thoroughly, top to bottom."},
  {q:"How was the second bird offered?", options:["For a burnt offering, according to the manner","As a peace offering","As food for the priests raw","Released alive over the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:10",verse:"And he shall offer the second for a burnt offering, according to the manner: and the priest shall make an atonement for him for his sin which he hath sinned, and it shall be forgiven him.",
   insight:"The second bird went up as a burnt offering, and he was forgiven. God's system always ended in mercy for the repentant."},
  {q:"If he could not afford the two birds, what was he to bring?", options:["The tenth part of an ephah of fine flour, with no oil and no frankincense","A loaf of leavened bread","A jar of olive oil","A handful of barley"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:11",verse:"But if he be not able to bring two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, then he that sinned shall bring for his offering the tenth part of an ephah of fine flour for a sin offering; he shall put no oil upon it, neither shall he put any frankincense thereon: for it is a sin offering.",
   insight:"A tenth of an ephah of flour, with no oil or frankincense, could atone. When the heart is broken, God accepts the humblest gift."},
  {q:"What did the priest do with the flour offering?", options:["Take his handful of it as a memorial, and burn it on the altar","Burn the whole tenth at once","Give it all back to the offerer","Mix it with water for the priests"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:12",verse:"Then shall he bring it to the priest, and the priest shall take his handful of it, even a memorial thereof, and burn it on the altar, according to the offerings made by fire unto the LORD: it is a sin offering.",
   insight:"A handful burned as a memorial on the altar. God remembers the repentant sinner with favor."},
  {q:"What became of the remnant of the flour sin offering?", options:["It shall be the priest's, as a meat offering","It was thrown outside the camp","It was given to the poor","It was burned entirely"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:13",verse:"And the priest shall make an atonement for him as touching his sin that he hath sinned in one of these, and it shall be forgiven him: and the remnant shall be the priest’s, as a meat offering.",
   insight:"The remnant belonged to the priest, as a meat offering. God feeds His servants through the repentance of His people."},
  {q:"To whom did the LORD speak about trespass in holy things?", options:["Moses","Aaron","The elders","The congregation"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:14",verse:"And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,",
   insight:"Again the LORD spoke to Moses, this time about trespasses against holy things. God teaches specifically because He cares specifically."},
  {q:"What was required for trespass in the holy things of the LORD?", options:["A ram without blemish, valued by shekels of silver after the shekel of the sanctuary","A bullock without price","Two doves and a lamb","Flour without measure"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:15",verse:"If a soul commit a trespass, and sin through ignorance, in the holy things of the LORD; then he shall bring for his trespass unto the LORD a ram without blemish out of the flocks, with thy estimation by shekels of silver, after the shekel of the sanctuary, for a trespass offering:",
   insight:"Trespass against holy things required a ram without blemish, valued in sanctuary shekels. What is taken from God must be repaid by His measure."},
  {q:"What extra was added when making amends for harm to holy things?", options:["The fifth part thereof, given unto the priest","A tenth part to the king","Double to the neighbor","Nothing extra at all"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:16",verse:"And he shall make amends for the harm that he hath done in the holy thing, and shall add the fifth part thereto, and give it unto the priest: and the priest shall make an atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering, and it shall be forgiven him.",
   insight:"The offender repaid the harm plus a fifth part. True repentance restores more than it took."},
  {q:"What was true of the soul who sinned without knowing it?", options:["Though he wist it not, yet is he guilty, and shall bear his iniquity","He was counted innocent","He was warned only once","His sin was forgotten"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:17",verse:"And if a soul sin, and commit any of these things which are forbidden to be done by the commandments of the LORD; though he wist it not, yet is he guilty, and shall bear his iniquity.",
   insight:"Even unknown transgression brought guilt. Ignorance of the law does not erase the debt."},
  {q:"What did the priest use to make atonement for sins of ignorance?", options:["A ram without blemish for a trespass offering","A young bullock","Two turtledoves","Fine flour with oil"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:18",verse:"And he shall bring a ram without blemish out of the flock, with thy estimation, for a trespass offering, unto the priest: and the priest shall make an atonement for him concerning his ignorance wherein he erred and wist it not, and it shall be forgiven him.",
   insight:"The ram of the trespass offering made atonement for sins of ignorance. God covers even the wrongs we cannot trace."},
  {q:"How does verse 19 describe the trespasser?", options:["He hath certainly trespassed against the LORD","He hath done no real wrong","He is excused by his ignorance","He is free without offering"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:19",verse:"It is a trespass offering: he hath certainly trespassed against the LORD.",
   insight:"He hath certainly trespassed against the LORD. Honest verdicts about our sin open the door to honest grace."},
  {q:"What was the promised end of the priest's atonement?", options:["It shall be forgiven him","He must return next year","He waited outside the camp","His offering was set aside"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 5:13",verse:"And the priest shall make an atonement for him as touching his sin that he hath sinned in one of these, and it shall be forgiven him: and the remnant shall be the priest’s, as a meat offering.",
   insight:"It shall be forgiven him. The trespass offering ends where every true confession ends: forgiven."}
 ]}
]);
